<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93509" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβάσμ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Vett.Val.
			242.26
		</span></i>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			14
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdn.
			7.5.3
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σέβας</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>reverend, venerable, august</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.764b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				27.10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρὸς θεοὺς ς</span>.
				<i>reverence</i> for . ., <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				2.10.2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ptol.Ascal.
					p.395
				</span></i>
			 H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as epith.
			of the Roman Emperor, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβαστός</span>
			, <u>Augustus</u>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				834.6
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				2.3.3
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεβαστόν</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> οἱ -ώτατοι Καίσαρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CPR</u>
					37.15
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὅρκος</span>,
			oath taken by the genius of the Emperor, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				1.40.19
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβάσμια, τά</span>, <i>games in honour of the Emperor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				3.129
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">iii A.D.</span>, in form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβάσμεια</span>, but perh. rather <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβασμεῖα</span>, 
				contr.
			 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεβασμιεῖα</span>); also on coins, Head <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hist.Num.</u>
				2717
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				784
			</span></i>.</div>
